        "C07", "C14",
        "C08", "C11", "C13",
        "C03", "C09", "C12", "C15", "C22", "C26", "C27"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability measurement or IV-referenced AUC comparison is available.",
    "No query-specific solubility, permeability, first-pass metabolism, or efflux data are available; the low prior is physicochemical only.",
    "Structural transfer from analogs is qualitative; no exact match to the query's benzofuran-diaminopyrimidine-indole scaffold is present.",
    "Some positive records come from modified-release, fed, fasted, or disease-specific populations that may not match the query's unstated condition.",
    "GDC-0810 bioavailability is PBPK-predicted rather than clinically measured."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "All L1 gold records in the transferable contexts report absolute oral bioavailability at or above roughly 35-80%, and none provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20%. The physicochemical low prior is not endpoint proof and is outweighed by consistent high-F analog evidence, so F >= 20% is better supported."
}

